          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "One of the clearer use cases is to use this transformation to deal with consuming vector data types for a target relational database that does not support vector data types. For example, you cannot write such data types to relational databases such as Db2, SQL Server, or Oracle prior to 23ai. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "VectorToJsonConverter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " transformation provides a useful, yet simple way to address this difference by converting all vector data type fields in the event payload from their respective vector-specific logical semantic representation to JSON."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JDBC sink"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The primary benefit of using JSON is that databases that support a Json data type will store the representation natively. For relatinoal databases that do not have a native JSON data type, those will default to use their respective long text equivalent data types."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Another use case involves ease of use. The Kafka Connect API is not one that many people are often comfortable working with and being provided the data in a format that is more intuitive simply lowers the complexity. Since Debezium’s JSON semantic type is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "io.debezium.data.Json"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and its natively represented in the Kafka event structure as a string value, it’s very easy to quickly parse the JSON details using any JSON library."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Ease of use"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_use_cases",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
